=== TEST_DESIGN ===

D1. Per-destination Field -> Destination -> Sentinel mapping (11 routed
    + 1 exempt). Driven from e2eFixtureSentinels in e2e_test.go so a
    fixture change requires updating this mapping or the per-
    destination assertion loop fails.

| #  | Field                       | Destination          | Sink     | Wire value                         | Notes                                     |
|----|-----------------------------|----------------------|----------|------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------|
|  1 | LocationLatitude            | positions            | writer   | 37.7749 via Location compound      | Location compound flattens to lat+long    |
|  2 | InsideTemp                  | climate_snapshot     | writer   | 25.0 °C (identity SI for °C)       | unit_history pre-seeded with KindTemp=°C  |
|  3 | Locked                      | security_event       | writer   | bool true                          | router Entry.Column == "" (event-shaped)  |
|  4 | DiTorqueActualF             | motor_snapshot       | writer   | 100.5 (UnitKindNone)               | identity pass-through                     |
|  5 | TpmsLastSeenPressureTimeFl  | tire_pressure_snap.  | writer   | 1714896000.0 (epoch sec, float)    | UnitKindNone — writer owns ts conversion  |
|  6 | MediaNowPlayingTitle        | media_snapshot       | writer   | "E2E Test Track"                   | string pass-through                       |
|  7 | ServiceMode                 | safety_snapshot      | writer   | bool true                          | bool pass-through                         |
|  8 | BatteryHeaterOn             | charging_telemetry   | writer   | bool true                          | bool pass-through                         |
|  9 | BrakePedal                  | drive_telemetry      | writer   | bool true                          | bool pass-through                         |
| 10 | AutomaticBlindSpotCamera    | signal_log           | writer   | bool true                          | only-signal_log dest (no also_signal_log) |
| 11 | SettingDistanceUnit         | unit_history         | histrepo | DistanceUnit_DistanceUnitKilometers | short-circuits to histRepo.Record         |
|  - | (none)                      | location_snapshot    | EXEMPT   | n/a                                | Decision #4 escape — 0 routes today       |

D2. Decision #2 escape hatch — DB layer
    Per the prompt's escape clause "If neither [pgxmock nor
    testcontainers] is available, fall back to in-memory recording
    fakes for writers and ASSERT the writer was called with the
    expected (vehicle_id, ts, field, value) tuple — this drops the
    actual DB INSERT verification but keeps the routing + observer
    chain exercised."  e2e_helpers_test.go provides
    *e2eRecordingWriter implementing router.Writer and capturing
    every Write call's (codec.Atomic, router.Entry) tuple in a
    mutex-protected slice. Per-destination assertions read
    callForField(field) for the sentinel field and verify
    Entry.Destination, VIN, EmittedAt, and Value.

D3. Decision #4 escape hatch — DestLocationSnapshot exemption
    The location_snapshots table is populated by a separate
    geocoding worker (NOT by the telemetry pipeline). routing.yaml
    has 0 entries with `dest: location_snapshot` (verified in A5).
    The 11/12 coverage is therefore COMPLETE for the pipeline path.
    Test 3 contains an explicit canary that asserts
    DestLocationSnapshot writer received zero calls — if a future
    routing.yaml change adds a `dest: location_snapshot` entry,
    that assertion will fail and the next prompt author will know
    to extend e2eFixtureSentinels.

D4. Decision #6 adaptation — production wiring smoke test
    Decision #6 references "a tiny test-only buildPipeline helper
    extracted in 0050". That helper does NOT exist — phase-42a/0050
    inlined the wiring directly in cmd/teslasync/main.go (verified
    in A3). Adapted: TestE2EPipeline_ProductionWiringSmoke
    replicates the SAME constructor SHAPE — same 12 router.Destination
    keys, same teslapipeline.New + normalize.New call sequence —
    using in-memory recording fakes. The existing source-grep tests
    in cmd/teslasync/main_pipeline_wiring_test.go cover that
    cmd/teslasync ITSELF still uses this shape; the e2e test proves
    the shape COMPILES + WORKS end-to-end.

D5. Decision #1 fixture choice — in-code proto.Marshal vs binary file
    e2eFixturePayload() in e2e_helpers_test.go builds an
    *ftproto.Payload literal with all 12 sentinel datums and
    proto.Marshal()s it on every call (cheap — single proto
    payload). No testdata/sample_payload.bin file is created. This
    keeps the fixture diffable in code review and avoids binary
    blobs in the tree. The prompt's allowed-files clause permits
    the binary path — choosing in-code is a deliberate trade-off
    for readability.

D6. Test pace
    All 3 top-level tests use t.Parallel(). The headline test
    further parallelises every per-destination sub-test. Total
    runtime under -race on Windows: 3.151s (see GATE G3 below) —
    well under the 10s "fast suite" target and the 30s hard limit.

D7. Observer signals map invariant
    The headline test asserts the live-store callback's signals
    map contains EVERY field the payload produced — 12 expected
    keys: SettingDistanceUnit, LocationLatitude, LocationLongitude
    (free rider from Location compound), InsideTemp, Locked,
    DiTorqueActualF, TpmsLastSeenPressureTimeFl, MediaNowPlayingTitle,
    ServiceMode, BatteryHeaterOn, BrakePedal, AutomaticBlindSpotCamera.
    This defends the phase-42a/0030 contract that the observer sees
    the post-route slice with SI substitutions applied, no field
    lost between the route loop and observer fan-out.


=== IMPLEMENTATION ===

I1. Files added (newline counts via `Get-Content | Measure-Object -Line`)

  internal/tesla_pipeline/e2e_helpers_test.go   518 lines
  internal/tesla_pipeline/e2e_test.go           633 lines
  TOTAL                                        1151 lines (test code only)

I2. e2e_helpers_test.go contents
    - constants: e2eVehicleID=4242, e2eVIN="5YJ3E1EA0KFE2EE2E",
      e2eEmittedAt=2026-05-06T12:00:00Z (fixed for ts equality
      assertions)
    - *e2eRecordingWriter implements router.Writer; captures every
      Write call's (Atomic, Entry, recordedAt) tuple, exposes
      callsCopy() and callForField(name) for assertions
    - *e2eHistRepo implements unithistory.Repo; preSeedActiveUnits
      seeds KindDistance=km, KindTemperature=C, KindPressure=bar so
      InsideTemp converts cleanly via units.ToSI
    - 6 callback fakes for SideEffectsObserver:
        e2eLiveStore (LiveSignalStore.UpdateAll)
        e2eHistoryWriter (SignalHistoryWriter.Append)
        e2eFSM (FSMHandler.ProcessSignals)
        e2eSessions (SessionTracker.ProcessSignals)
        e2eAlerts (AlertEvaluator.Evaluate)
        e2eVINResolver (VINResolver.VINByID — happy-path resolves
                        e2eVIN -> e2eVehicleID)
        e2eSSE (BroadcastSSEFunc closure adapter)
    - All fake types prefixed `e2e` to avoid collision with the
      existing fakeXxx types in side_effects_observer_test.go
      (same package teslapipeline)
    - e2eFixturePayload() builds *ftproto.Payload with all 12
      sentinel datums and returns proto.Marshal(payload)

I3. e2e_test.go contents
    - TestE2EPipeline_AllDestinationsAndObserverFire
        Decision #4 implementation. 11 per-destination sub-tests
        (driven from e2eFixtureSentinels) + 6 value-correctness
        sub-tests (InsideTemp SI conversion, BrakePedal/Title/Brake
        pass-through, all 6 observer callbacks each invoked once,
        observer signals map covers all 12 routed fields).
    - TestE2EPipeline_MalformedPayloadIsolatesFailure
        Decision #5 implementation. Sends []byte{0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff}
        (truncated, forces a malformed-varint decode error rather
        than the "empty bytes are valid Payload" false positive).
        Asserts errors.Is(err, normalize.ErrPayloadDrop) AND every
        writer / observer / histRepo received 0 calls.
    - TestE2EPipeline_ProductionWiringSmoke
        Decision #6 adapted. Replicates cmd/teslasync wiring shape
        with in-memory fakes; asserts:
          - writers map has exactly 12 entries (cmd/teslasync's set)
          - router.New succeeds
          - teslapipeline.New returns non-nil observer
          - normalize.New returns non-nil pipeline
          - fixture payload reaches every routed destination
          - observer fan-out fires
          - DestLocationSnapshot writer received 0 calls (canary
            for the Decision #4 exemption)


